From: Toon Verwaest <verwaest@chromium.org>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 16:30:54 +0200
Subject: [parser] Parse yield operand as AssignmentExpression

The operand of a `YieldExpression` is unconditionally an
`AssignmentExpression` and cannot be a destructuring pattern or arrow
parameter list.

Previously, `ParseYieldExpression` called
`ParseAssignmentExpressionCoverGrammar()`, leaving expression errors in
the operand (such as `{a = 42}`) unvalidated in the enclosing scope, so
an outer `[yield {a = 42}] = []` cleared the expression error during
`ValidateAsPattern()` and reported `Invalid destructuring assignment
target` instead of `Invalid shorthand property initializer`.

Use `ParseAssignmentExpression()` instead.

